    <div aria-label="Ingredients one and two"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-reason"> <div class="gp-num">1</div> <h3>Ashwagandha</h3> <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Ashwagandha" loading="lazy" width="900" height="600"> <span class="gp-dose">Look for ~600mg, standardised</span> <p>The most-studied of the group. It's an adaptogen &mdash; it works on the stress side of the equation, and chronically high stress hormone is one of the biggest things quietly working against a man's testosterone. This is the one you'll see cited most, and for good reason. The catch: most products sneak in 100&ndash;150mg and call it a day. The research doses are higher.</p> </div> <div class="gp-reason"> <div class="gp-num">2</div> <h3>Tongkat Ali</h3> <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Tongkat Ali" loading="lazy" width="900" height="600"> <span class="gp-dose">Look for ~400mg</span> <p>Used across Southeast Asia for generations and now the most-researched name in the men's category specifically. Where ashwagandha works on stress, tongkat is the one people reach for when they want the "drive" side back. Quality varies wildly &mdash; extract ratio and dose are everything, and cheap versions are barely there.</p> </div></div></div>
